  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ALONSO DE BRICEÑO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alonso de Briceño is a Catholic bishop known for his unwavering commitment to the Church and its teachings, and for establishing numerous institutions to benefit his people."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alonso de Briceño is a Roman Catholic prelate who served as the Bishop of Caracas, known for his dedication to the Church and his work in establishing schools, hospitals, and orphanages."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VATICAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Vatican is the center of the Catholic Church, where Alonso de Briceño submitted his resignation as Bishop of Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BISHOP OF CARACAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bishop of Caracas is a religious position held by Alonso de Briceño, responsible for the spiritual guidance of the Catholic faithful in Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARACAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caracas is a city in Venezuela where Alonso de Briceño served as the Bishop and later retired as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLY SEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Holy See is the governing body of the Catholic Church, to which Alonso de Briceño submitted his resignation as Bishop of Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPANISH MINISTRY OF LABOR AND SOCIAL SECURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Spanish Ministry of Labor and Social Security confirmed that Alonso de Briceño began collecting a pension of €2,500 per month."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATHER JUAN CARLOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Father Juan Carlos is a longtime colleague of Alonso de Briceño, expressing surprise at his decision to resign and retire."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIA RODRIGUEZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maria Rodriguez is a local resident who claims to have spotted Alonso de Briceño at a recent bingo night, noting his happiness in his new life as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. ELENA VASQUEZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Elena Vasquez is a theologian at the University of Madrid, commenting on the implications of Alonso de Briceño's decision to retire."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF MADRID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Madrid is the institution where Dr. Elena Vasquez teaches, providing a platform for her theological insights."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17TH CENTURY CARACAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"17th century Caracas is the setting where Alonso de Briceño lived and served as a priest before becoming the Bishop of Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHOLIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Catholic community is the group of believers who Alonso de Briceño served as a priest and bishop, now struggling to come to terms with his retirement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHURCH HIERARCHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Church hierarchy is the system within the Catholic Church that recognized Alonso de Briceño as a suitable candidate for the Bishop of Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCHOOLS, HOSPITALS, ORPHANAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Schools, Hospitals, and Orphanages are the institutions established by Alonso de Briceño during his tenure as Bishop of Caracas to serve the needs of the poor and marginalized."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLIP-FLOPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flip-flops are mentioned as part of Alonso de Briceño's new life as a pensioner, symbolizing his leisure lifestyle."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOLF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Golf is mentioned as one of Alonso de Briceño's favorite pastimes in his new life as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bingo is mentioned as one of Alonso de Briceño's favorite pastimes in his new life as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beaches are mentioned as part of Alonso de Briceño's new life as a pensioner, where he spends his days lounging."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitre is the ecclesiastical headgear that Alonso de Briceño traded for a life of leisure as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASSOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cassock is the clerical garment that Alonso de Briceño traded for a life of leisure as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOLDEN YEARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Golden Years refer to the period of leisure and relaxation that Alonso de Briceño is pursuing as a pensioner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pension is the financial benefit that Alonso de Briceño is receiving after his resignation as Bishop of Caracas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHURCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Church is the religious institution to which Alonso de Briceño dedicated himself, emphasizing its teachings and the establishment of institutions based on its values."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BISHOP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bishop is the religious position held by Alonso de Briceño, characterized by his leadership and dedication to the welfare of his community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTITUTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Institutions refer to the various organizations and establishments Alonso de Briceño founded during his tenure as Bishop, highlighting his commitment to the welfare of his people."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"People refers to the community that Alonso de Briceño served and worked to improve through his institutions and teachings."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0329</data>
    </node>
